acceptance_criteria: "pnpm why postcss resolves only patched versions >=8.5.18; GitHub Dependabot alert #43 is closed; lockfile supply-chain policy, audit, static analysis, exact coverage, compatibility, package smoke, and exact-head DeepScan/CodeFactor gates pass; fix ships in the next PR and is linked from the alert follow-up lineage."
parent: pm-qwoy
severity: high
environment: pnpm-lock.yaml; transitive development dependency postcss 8.5.16 via vite 7.3.5 and vitest 4.1.10
repro_steps: "Read GitHub Dependabot alert 43 and run pnpm why postcss; current graph resolves one version, postcss 8.5.16, while the first patched version is 8.5.18."
resolution: Upgraded dependencies and Action pins and constrained PostCSS to its patched range.
expected_result: No installed dependency remains vulnerable to GHSA-r28c-9q8g-f849 and security workflows use current immutable actions.
actual_result: "PostCSS resolves at a patched version; pnpm audit, CodeQL, Semgrep, Trivy, TruffleHog, and CI are green."
component: dependency supply chain
regression: false
customer_impact: Development-only transitive exposure; crafted sourceMappingURL input processed by affected tooling could disclose arbitrary .map files.
